// smoke: hotkey-body input-context sugar — per docs/specs/Havel.md
//        "Input Shortcuts (Implicit Input Statements)".
//        Inside a hotkey block, bare input commands work without `>`:
//        strings send text, `lmb` clicks, `{Key}` sends a key.
//        Parse+register only: hotkey callbacks don't fire in this harness,
//        and input host functions degrade gracefully without /dev/uinput.
//        Expected: script registers the hotkey and exits 0
//        (havel --run exits when the script completes).
x = 0
F24 => {
  "Hello"
  lmb
  {Home}
}
x = 1
assert(x == 1, "hotkey block with implicit input commands must parse and register")
// hotkey registration enters the launcher keep-alive loop; exit explicitly
process.exit(0)
